 ✅ What is docker-compose? Its usages ?

Docker Compose is a tool for managing and running multi-container Docker applications. Instead of starting containers individually with multiple docker run commands, Docker Compose allows you to manage them together using a single configuration file.

docker-compose up/down  
docker-compose.yaml 





• Simplifies Multi-Container Setup
If your application needs multiple components (e.g., a web server, database, cache), you can define them in one file and start them together.
• Environment Consistency
The same configuration works across development, testing, and production environments.
• Networking Made Easy
Compose automatically creates a network for your services so they can communicate by name.
• Reusable Configurations
You can version-control the docker-compose.yml file and share it with your team.
• Scaling
You can easily scale services up or down using: docker-compose up

